{
  "tema": 8601,
  "slug": "bien-intensificador",
  "titulo": "Using bien as an intensifier (very)",
  "subtitulo": "Bien rico, bien tarde: bien = muy, and very Mexican.",
  "foto": "t05.jpg",
  "regla": "Bien before an adjective or adverb means very: bien rico, bien tarde. Bien never changes; the adjective agrees. Bien mal = very bad.",
  "comparada_kwiziq": "2026-10-10",
  "secciones": [
    {
      "id": "regla",
      "titulo": "The rule",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "**Bien** can work as an intensifier meaning _very, quite_, before **adjectives** and some **adverbs**. It works just like **muy** or **bastante**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "formula",
          "partes": [
            "**bien**",
            "adjective / adverb"
          ]
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "**Bien** never changes; the adjective after it agrees with the noun: **bien delgada**, **bien gordos**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "You can even say **bien mal** for _very bad_."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "This use is a bit more colloquial than **muy**, and it's very common in Mexico."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Tip: if you can say **muy**, you can usually say **bien** and sound like a local."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ejemplos",
      "titulo": "Examples",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "ejemplos",
          "lista": [
            {
              "es": "Ayer comí unos tacos ==bien== ricos.",
              "en": "Yesterday I ate some really tasty tacos."
            },
            {
              "es": "Tus hijos son ==bien== serios.",
              "en": "Your kids are very serious."
            },
            {
              "es": "Lo tengo ==bien== amarrado.",
              "en": "I've got it tied up tight."
            },
            {
              "es": "Estás ==bien== flaca. Tu dieta funciona.",
              "en": "You're really thin. Your diet's working."
            },
            {
              "es": "Me dieron cita ==bien== rápido.",
              "en": "They gave me an appointment really quickly."
            },
            {
              "es": "Llegamos ==bien== tarde a la fiesta.",
              "en": "We got to the party really late."
            },
            {
              "es": "—¿Cómo está Beto? —Está ==bien mal== después de la noticia.",
              "en": "\"How's Beto?\" \"He's in really bad shape after the news.\""
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "trampa",
      "titulo": "The trap",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "pares",
          "lista": [
            {
              "filas": [
                {
                  "v": "mal",
                  "t": "Están bienes cansados."
                },
